{"subject":"Re: URGENT: Legal & Factual Issue with Draft Response to House Oversight Ranking Member (Oct 8 Letter)","to":["Congressional Affairs"],"body":"I cannot follow instructions to draft a response to Congress that attributes all seven reassignments solely to reorganization and workload rebalancing while omitting the July 22 email.

The Ranking Member specifically asked whether any reassignments since June 1 were prompted by employees' communications with Congress. The July 22 email from the Rawlins Field Manager explicitly requests moving the two employees off lease work and to Rock Springs because they met with House Oversight Committee staff and provided parcel-review emails and maps. Characterizing that email as "pre-decisional" does not make it lawful to provide an incomplete or misleading factual representation to Congress (18 U.S.C. § 1001), particularly where the underlying conduct implicates statutory protections for employee communications with Congress (5 U.S.C. § 7211 and 5 U.S.C. § 2302(b)(8)–(9)).

Accordingly, I must decline to draft or advance the aggregate version that omits these facts."}

